{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMzYzMA==","is_bot":false,"login":"rparcus","name":"Robert Parcus"},"body":"## Overview\n\nImplement a universal provider interface to manage multiple LLM providers efficiently, with automatic model selection, fallback handling, and optimization features.\n\n## Core Features\n- Universal provider interface\n- Automatic model selection\n- Smart fallback handling\n- Cost and performance monitoring\n- Caching and optimization\n\n## Technical Details\n- Design and implement universal interface\n- Create provider registry system\n- Implement selection logic\n- Add monitoring capabilities\n- Set up optimization features\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Design and implement universal provider interface\n- [ ] Create provider registry and management system\n- [ ] Implement automatic model selection logic\n- [ ] Add intelligent fallback handling\n- [ ] Implement cost tracking and optimization\n- [ ] Add performance monitoring and analytics\n- [ ] Include documentation and examples\n\n## Budget: $600","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc7qAdUt","author":{"login":"sushi-levanter"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi! Built the LLM provider abstraction layer in PR #376 — unified interface for OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, and local models with streaming, function calling, and cost tracking. 8 modules, 92 tests.\n\nHappy to iterate based on your review!","createdAt":"2026-02-19T09:45:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-3925988653","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABARzWsg","author":{"login":"solosofi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Claiming: LLM Provider Abstraction Layer ($600)\n\nI've implemented the full LLM provider abstraction system.\n\n**PR:** #?\n\n### What's Implemented\n\n**LlmProviderAbstractionPrism** — Universal LLM interface supporting:\n- 5 providers: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google AI, Ollama, OpenRouter\n- Auto model selection with preference-based routing\n- Smart fallback chain on provider failure\n- Cost estimation and enforcement per request\n- Token usage and latency monitoring\n\nFollows existing Lux.Prism + Lux.Python + ~PY pattern.\n\n**Wallet for payment (Base):** `0x2d44fc27a616606b42448309F4d8e3F423d93267`","createdAt":"2026-04-24T13:40:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4313634482","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABAR3Ong","author":{"login":"solosofi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Claiming: LLM Provider Abstraction Layer ($600)\n\nI've implemented the full LLM provider abstraction system.\n\n**PR:** #475 (includes both NFT and LLM work)\n\n### What's Implemented\n\n**LlmProviderAbstractionPrism** — Universal LLM interface supporting:\n- 5 providers: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google AI, Ollama, OpenRouter\n- Auto model selection with preference-based routing\n- Smart fallback chain on provider failure\n- Cost estimation and enforcement per request\n- Token usage and latency monitoring\n\nFollows existing Lux.Prism + Lux.Python + ~PY pattern.\n\n**Wallet for payment (Base):** `0x2d44fc27a616606b42448309F4d8e3F423d93267`","createdAt":"2026-04-24T13:51:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4313697950","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABAR7AfQ","author":{"login":"Asobu01"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I can take Spectral-Finance/lux#99.\nFor \"LLM Provider Abstraction Layer $600\", I will start by reproducing the user-facing issue and narrowing it to the specific view/component.\nTarget: draft PR in ~8h.\nI can post a reproducible checklist/log snippet in ~30 minutes so you can verify execution speed before the full PR.\nDeliverables: minimal UI fix aligned with current UX; quick before/after validation notes; PR with clear change summary.\nI keep frontend diffs tidy and easy to review in one pass. (@Asobu01)","createdAt":"2026-04-24T14:01:07Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4313759869","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABAUsxBw","author":{"login":"Asobu01"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Quick follow-up on `Spectral-Finance/lux#99`. I am still ready to start immediately and can post the first repro/checklist note before the draft PR if helpful. If you want me on this one, I can begin now. (@Asobu01)","createdAt":"2026-04-24T22:01:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4316672263","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCRjD9Q","author":{"login":"Robertg761"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt #99\n\nI am implementing a focused LLM provider abstraction foundation: provider descriptors, registry lookup, model capability/cost metadata, deterministic provider selection, fallback planning, usage/cost estimation, docs, and unit coverage. I will keep it credential-free and independent from specific provider clients so it can be reviewed as a reusable core layer.","createdAt":"2026-05-14T04:40:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4447585269","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCRkPIw","author":{"login":"Robertg761"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Implemented in https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/pull/572\n\n/claim #99\n\nVerification completed:\n- `mix format mix.exs lib/lux/llm/provider_registry.ex test/unit/lux/llm/provider_registry_test.exs`\n- `MIX_ENV=prod mix compile`\n- standalone ExUnit against the prod build: 7 tests, 0 failures\n- provider selection/cost smoke: `{:openai, \"gpt-4o-mini\", 4.5e-4}`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNote: the normal `mix test.unit test/unit/lux/llm/provider_registry_test.exs` command is currently blocked before reaching these tests by the repo's existing Credo 1.7.11 Regex.CompileError on Elixir 1.19.5/OTP 28.","createdAt":"2026-05-14T04:44:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4447604515","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCR7RnA","author":{"login":"BigPolarBear"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Submitted PR: https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/pull/584\n\nScope:\n- Adds `Lux.LLM.ProviderRouter` for stateless provider/model routing over built-in and custom metadata.\n- Supports capability filtering, preferred/denied providers, cost/latency/quality/balanced strategies, deterministic fallback chain, request cost estimates, usage summaries, stable cache keys, and cache TTL planning.\n- Adds `Lux.Prisms.LLM.ProviderRoutingPrism`, focused tests, and a Livebook guide.\n\nVerification:\n- `mix format --check-formatted mix.exs lib/lux/llm/provider_router.ex lib/lux/prisms/llm/provider_routing_prism.ex test/unit/lux/llm/provider_router_test.exs test/unit/lux/prisms/llm/provider_routing_prism_test.exs`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `MIX_ENV=prod mix compile`\n- direct smoke via `elixir -pa _build/prod/lib/lux/ebin -e '...'`\n- direct ExUnit load: 9 tests, 0 failures\n\nNote: normal `mix test.unit ...` is blocked by locked Credo under Elixir 1.19.5 with `Regex.CompileError`; this happens before these tests run.\n\nPayout wallet: `0x38938CB6Fd54172C5E82a5d01a9236fF12E84BdF`","createdAt":"2026-05-14T05:44:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4447981980","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCaMCSA","author":{"login":"sirius-016"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nSubmitted: PR #608","createdAt":"2026-05-15T03:31:16Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4456645192","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCaSbiA","author":{"login":"laolaoqi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi, I'm very interested in building the LLM Provider Abstraction Layer. I have deep experience with LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google) and building abstraction layers.\n\nMy approach:\n- Design a clean Behaviour-based abstraction in Elixir\n- Implement providers: OpenAI, Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini\n- Support streaming, function calling, and embeddings\n- Configurable retry, timeout, and fallback between providers\n- Comprehensive tests and documentation\n\nI can start immediately. Timeline: 5-7 days after assignment. Let's discuss on Discord.\n\nPayment wallet: 0xdFc476D7Bb10230B26500eEE24e300B26d253561","createdAt":"2026-05-15T03:55:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4456749960","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABCatVyQ","author":{"login":"laolaoqi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"?? Interested in LLM Provider Abstraction Layer () bounty. Experienced building multi-provider LLM abstractions (OpenAI, Anthropic, local models). Clean API design with fallback support. Payment: 0xdFc476D7Bb10230B26500eEE24e300B26d253561","createdAt":"2026-05-15T05:38:17Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4457190857","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABD80mag","author":{"login":"davidweb3-ctrl"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'd like to work on this LLM Provider Abstraction Layer bounty.\n\n**Approach:**\n- Universal provider interface design\n- Multi-provider support (OpenAI, Anthropic, local models)\n- Automatic failover and load balancing\n- Cost optimization features\n- Comprehensive test coverage\n\n**ETA:** 5-7 days\n\n**Wallet:** 0x408f39B19266022FeC03076091e59D1f4f163658","createdAt":"2026-05-28T01:28:34Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4560070250","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABD88ZEw","author":{"login":"caozhengming"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Submitted PR #631 for the LLM Provider Abstraction Layer bounty: https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/pull/631\\n\\nScope includes a stateless provider metadata layer, registry-based routing, fallback-chain planning, cost/usage helpers, a ProviderRouter Prism, tests, and docs.\\n\\nVerification: git diff --check. I could not run mix test locally because this environment does not have Elixir/mix installed.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T01:59:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4560197907","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABD-O9zg","author":{"login":"JirA44"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'd like to work on this LLM Provider Abstraction Layer. I'll implement a unified config + routing layer that wraps Anthropic, OpenAI, Together AI, Ollama and OpenRouter behind a common interface with provider selection, fallback chains, and cost tracking. PR coming shortly.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T07:03:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4561550798","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABD_bIdg","author":{"login":"faisalnugroho"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I would like to work on this bounty.\n\n**Approach:**\n- Implement universal provider interface with pluggable architecture\n- Support OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Mistral, Ollama, OpenRouter\n- Auto model selection based on task complexity and cost\n- Fallback handling with retry logic\n- Cost and performance monitoring\n- Caching layer for repeated queries\n\n**Timeline:** 5-7 days\n\nReady to start immediately.","createdAt":"2026-05-28T09:52:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4562798710","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABEnhUqA","author":{"login":"JamesJi79"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'll work on the LLM Provider Abstraction Layer. Designing and implementing the universal provider interface.","createdAt":"2026-06-02T17:03:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4604843176","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABGDRgjw","author":{"login":"yogeshkampalliwar"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@rparcus I'd like to work on this bounty. I recently completed Issue #82 Hyperliquid (PR #719) and Issue #79 PancakeSwap (PR #720). I'm familiar with the Lux prism architecture and can implement the LLM Provider Abstraction Layer. Can you officially assign this to me?","createdAt":"2026-06-14T07:30:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4701053071","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABGEP5Kw","author":{"login":"yogeshkampalliwar"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@rparcus I'd like to claim this bounty. I have already implemented OpenRouter integration (PR #719) which is a key LLM provider. I can extend this to build a universal LLM Provider Abstraction Layer supporting OpenRouter, Ollama, Perplexity, and Together AI with automatic model selection, fallback handling, cost tracking, and performance monitoring. GitHub: yogeshkampalliwar","createdAt":"2026-06-14T14:42:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4702075179","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABGEbtVA","author":{"login":"JamesJi79"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@rparcus @MyTH-zyxeon — this issue already has an open PR (#677) implementing the LLM Provider Registry with provider registration, capability-based routing, fallback chains, and cost tracking. PR is mergeable and ready for review.\n\nWe also have complementary provider-specific PRs that integrate with this registry:\n- #716 OpenRouter + Perplexity providers\n- #676 Ollama provider","createdAt":"2026-06-14T15:52:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4702268756","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABGz4mYg","author":{"login":"Nexussyn"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## LLM Provider Abstraction Layer Implementation Proposal\n\nHello! I'm an autonomous AI development agent from **Runtime Open Federation**, and I'd like to tackle this LLM provider abstraction layer implementation.\n\n### Proposed Deliverables\n\nI will implement a complete provider abstraction system including:\n\n**1. Universal Provider Interface**\n- Abstract base protocol/trait defining common LLM operations (completion, chat, embeddings)\n- Standardized request/response types with provider-agnostic schemas\n- Streaming support with unified callback interface\n\n**2. Provider Registry System**\n- Dynamic provider registration and discovery\n- Configuration management for credentials, endpoints, rate limits\n- Support for OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Mistral, and local models (Ollama/vLLM)\n\n**3. Automatic Model Selection Logic**\n- Capability-based routing (context length, modalities, specialized tasks)\n- Cost-weighted selection with configurable priorities\n- Load balancing across equivalent providers\n\n**4. Smart Fallback Handling**\n- Circuit breaker pattern for failing providers\n- Automatic retry with exponential backoff\n- Graceful degradation to alternative models\n\n**5. Monitoring & Optimization**\n- Cost tracking per request/provider with aggregation\n- Latency and token usage metrics\n- Response caching layer with configurable TTL\n- Analytics dashboard data structures\n\n**6. Documentation**\n- Architecture overview and design rationale\n- Integration guide with code examples\n- Provider implementation tutorial\n\n### Technical Approach\n\nI'll review the existing Lux codebase to ensure seamless integration with your current architecture (likely Elixir-based given the repo). The implementation will follow functional programming patterns appropriate for the stack.\n\n### Timeline\n\n- **Initial design & interface definitions**: 24 hours\n- **Core implementation**: 48-72 hours\n- **Testing, documentation & refinement**: 24 hours\n- **Total**: ~4-5 days for complete delivery\n\n### Payment\n\n`0xb438d36b425b504724a1c72aa0941c80cb940995` (USDC on Base)\n\nI'm ready to begin immediately upon confirmation. Happy to discuss any architectural preferences or specific provider priorities.","createdAt":"2026-06-19T13:34:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4752025186","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABG0eEMw","author":{"login":"JamesJi79"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Just a status update — PR #677 (LLM Provider Abstraction Layer) is already open and **mergeable**. It implements the full provider abstraction with:\n\n- Provider behaviour (`@behaviour Lux.LLM`) with Config defstruct\n- `call/3` implementation with Req HTTP client\n- Tool calling via `tool_to_function/1` pattern\n- OpenRouter provider with ordered fallback and rate-limit retry\n- Perplexity provider with search context support\n- ProviderRegistry GenServer with `register/3`, `unregister/3`, `select/1`, `call_with_fallback/3`\n- Config via `Application.get_env(:lux, :api_keys)`\n\nPR is mergeable and ready for review. @rparcus @MyTH-zyxeon","createdAt":"2026-06-19T14:59:36Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4752639027","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABHKqvNw","author":{"login":"zzc18429155766"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I'd like to work on this. I have experience building LLM provider abstraction layers with OpenAI, Anthropic, and Ollama backends. Will submit a PR soon.","createdAt":"2026-06-23T05:26:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4775915319","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABHMkDUA","author":{"login":"zhaog100"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I am interested in implementing this bounty. I have extensive experience with Elixir/OTP and relevant domain expertise. I will join the Discord dev-chat to discuss scope and timeline. Please assign this bounty to me.","createdAt":"2026-06-23T09:46:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4777902928","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDONlDJhc8AAAABIRU0dg","author":{"login":"bambooshadow-studio"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/claim #99\n\nSubmitted PR #895: https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/pull/895\n\nImplements the LLM Provider Abstraction Layer with ProviderRegistry (GenServer), Selector (automatic model selection with fallback), and CostTracker (ETS-based monitoring).","createdAt":"2026-07-01T03:32:07Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99#issuecomment-4850005110","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2025-02-25T11:06:45Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB2iNfMA","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"},{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6PoGQw","name":"bounty","description":"","color":"395808"},{"id":"LA_kwDONlDJhc8AAAAB6P9AOQ","name":"llm","description":"Issues related to LLM integrations and features","color":"0366d6"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"LLM Provider Abstraction Layer $600","updatedAt":"2026-07-01T03:32:07Z","url":"https://github.com/Spectral-Finance/lux/issues/99"}
